    "notes": "In this puzzle, some of the answers are one letter too long for the spaces. In those cases, enter either the first or last letter into a gray square. When you are finished, every gray square will have a letter in it, and when read from left to right and top to bottom, they will spell Laurence J. Peter's definition of a censor. On-line solvers need to print the grid with blacks squares set as gray (Edit menu, Options, Printing tab, Ink saver option)."
